# Sanction & Forgive: requests for a booking system's developers (VS Code REST Client, JetBrains HTTP Client).
# Every name here is fictional. The API: docs/api.md; its machine-readable description: GET /openapi/v1.json.
# What to do with each answer: docs/decisions.md.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Is it up, and are the lists loaded? (200 once the first load is done)
GET {{baseUrl}}/readyz

### The lists, their versions and how fresh they are
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/status
Accept: application/json

### Every list with its state, record count, last update and publisher (for a status screen)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sources
Accept: application/json

### One shipment: a receiver, a company and an address, each optional (at least one), up to 300 characters.
# reference: your own id for this check (1-64 letters, digits and . _ : / -), echoed back and the key to the audit
# log. Never put personal data in it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/screenings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "reference": "BOOKING-2026-000123",
  "receiverName": "Ivan Petrovich Sokolov",
  "companyName": "Northwind Trading LLC",
  "address": "12 Fictional Street, Moscow, Russia"
}

### A Cyrillic company name: matched against Latin and Cyrillic aliases alike
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/screenings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "reference": "BOOKING-2026-000124",
  "companyName": "ООО «Северный Ветер»"
}

### A batch: NDJSON in, NDJSON out (a header, a result or error line per record, an end line). Read the answer as
# it comes; check the end line: "truncated": true means send again from "nextLine". One stream at a time (429 with
# Retry-After otherwise). A few hundred records a stream keeps it simple; see samples/screen_batch.py.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/screenings/stream
Content-Type: application/x-ndjson
Accept: application/x-ndjson

{"reference":"BATCH-1-1","companyName":"Northwind Trading LLC","address":"Hamburg, Germany"}
{"reference":"BATCH-1-2","receiverName":"Anna Kowalska","address":"ul. Fikcyjna 5, Warszawa"}
{"reference":"BATCH-1-3","companyName":"Bluefield Logistics Ltd"}
